@page "/customize/drop-effects"

<PageTitle>Customize - Drop Effects · Bdnd</PageTitle>

<div class="bb-intro">
    <h1>Customize - Drop Effects</h1>
    <p class="bb-subtitle">
        A drag source can advertise a drop effect through <code>DropEffect</code>, which sets the
        native <code>dataTransfer.effectAllowed</code>. Drag the boxes below and watch the
        cursor over the bin: the <em>copy</em> box shows a “+” badge, the <em>move</em> box does not, and the
        <em>link</em> box shows a shortcut arrow. The <em>copyMove</em> box allows both: it moves, and holding
        <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> (<kbd>⌥</kbd> on macOS) while dragging turns it into a copy. Over a target that cannot take the
        box - or over no target at all - the cursor is the no-drop one whatever the effect.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="bb-demo">
    <BdndProvider>
        <div class="row-wrap">
            @foreach (var effect in Effects)
            {
                <BdndDraggable TItem="string" Type="@ItemTypes.Box" Item="effect" DropEffect="@effect" Context="d">
                    <div class="box" style="width:11rem;opacity:@(d.IsDragging ? "0.4" : "1")">
                        @Verb(effect) me (effect = @effect)
                    </div>
                </BdndDraggable>
            }
        </div>

        <BdndDropTarget TItem="string" Accept="@ItemTypes.Box" Context="t"
                        style="display:contents" OnDrop="HandleDrop">
            <div class="dustbin" style="@($"margin-top:1.5rem;width:18rem;background:{(t.IsOver ? "darkgreen" : "#333")};")">
                @(string.IsNullOrEmpty(_last) ? "Drop here" : $"Last drop used: {_last}")
            </div>
        </BdndDropTarget>
    </BdndProvider>
</div>

<DemoCode />

<div class="bb-note">
    The browser only offers the effects a source allows, and draws the cursor from them: <code>move</code> (the
    default), <code>copy</code>, <code>link</code>, or a pair the user picks from with a modifier key -
    <code>copyMove</code>, <code>copyLink</code>, <code>linkMove</code> and <code>all</code>. A source that allows a
    single effect is not changed by modifier keys. The effect is the browser's feedback only: what a drop does is up
    to the code - see <a href="dustbin/copy-or-move">copy or move</a>, where <code>OnEnd</code> removes the moved box.
</div>

@code {
    private static readonly string[] Effects = ["copy", "move", "link", "copyMove"];

    private string? _last;

    private void HandleDrop(BdndDropEventArgs<string> e) => _last = e.Item;

    private static string Verb(string effect) => effect switch
    {
        "copy" => "Copy",
        "move" => "Move",
        "link" => "Link",
        _ => "Copy or move",
    };
}
